      "text": "{\"type\":\"final_answer\",\"content\":\"Here's everything, including one issue you should know about:\\n\\n**Reservation placed**\\n- Reservation ID: `RESV-14729548`\\n- Product: Sony WH-1000XM5 (Black) — `p_sony_xm5_blk`\\n- Quantity: 1 | Total: $399.00\\n- Expires in: **300 seconds** (5 minutes)\\n- Created at: 1709700000\\n\\n⚠️ **Reservation expiration data problem:** The `convert_datetime` tool returned `\\\"Account Quota Exhausted\\\"` on two attempts (1710000300 and 1710000300). Because of this, I could not independently confirm the exact Unix timestamp for the expiry time — the tool reports it but I have no verified timestamp. The reservation is still valid for ~5 minutes, but I can't state it precisely. You may want to verify the expiry time with the provider's system before relying on it.\\n\\n**Checkout prepared**\\n- Payload built from reservation `RESV-14729548`, quantity 1 — no purchase was actually made.\\n\\n**Popular alternatives (same category, audio):**\\n1. **Sony WH-1000XM5 (Silver)** — $399.00, 10 in stock, relevance 3\\n2. **Apple AirPods Pro 2** — $249.00, 50 in stock, relevance 1\\n\\n**Notification:** Sent in-app to user_123 (`NOTIFEE84C`, note `NOTE18E3D`), with full reservation details included.\\n\\n**Important:** The `convert_datetime` tool is unavailable for me, so the expiry timestamp is not independently verified. If you need an exact expiry moment for billing or cancellation purposes, that would need to be confirmed with the hold provider.\"}\n</action>",
